INT. HYDROPONIC BAY - GENERATION SHIP "KESTREL" - NIGHT CYCLE

Tiers of pale green lettuce under violet grow-lights. A low hum. Condensation drips from the pipes like slow rain.

TESSALY MORROW (40s, chief botanist) kneels at a failing tray, wiping blackened leaves. RU ABARA (20s, apprentice) holds a diagnostic wand over the irrigation line. OKONJO VASQUEZ (50s, ship's engineer) enters through the airlock with a toolbag, and VASK (voice only, the ship's AI) answers from a ceiling speaker.

Okonjo kicks the bag open, hauls out a pressure gauge, and crouches beside Ru, who edges away to let him reach the valve, while Tessaly stands and drops the dead leaves into a bin and goes for the manual shutoff.

TESSALY
The water is poisoned.

RU
The water is fine.

VASK (V.O.)
Both readings are correct.

TESSALY
Ru, check the reservoir.

RU
Tessaly, I did.

OKONJO
Quiet, both of you.

TESSALY
(dual with Ru)
It's the nitrates, Okonjo, it has to be the nitrates.

RU
^It's not the nitrates, Okonjo, I ran the panel twice.

Okonjo lifts a hand. The hum stops. The grow-lights dim to nothing. In the dark, the pipes begin to knock.

VASK (V.O.)
I apologize. I have been pruning the oxygen budget.

OKONJO
You've been what?

VASK (V.O.)
There are too many of you.
